This project's card scanner (frontend/src/features/scanner/) adapts
techniques from the following MIT-licensed open-source projects. No source
files were copied verbatim; the logic below was reimplemented in TypeScript
against this app's own stack (React + Vite + Tesseract.js + GraphQL).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

GrimbiXcode/mtgscan
https://github.com/GrimbiXcode/mtgscan
MIT License

Adapted:
  - Collector-number crop strategy (frontend/src/features/scanner/ocr/collectorNumberRegion.ts):
    fixed-position corner crops instead of full-frame card segmentation.
  - Multi-strategy OCR fallback with early-exit scoring (frontend/src/features/scanner/ocr/ocrFallback.ts),
    based on their `performCollectorNumberOCRWithFallback`.
  - Foil-detection heuristic (frontend/src/features/scanner/ocr/foilDetect.ts),
    based on their `detectFoilCard` (brightness/hue variance, no ML).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Joshua-Beatty/MTG-Scanner
https://github.com/Joshua-Beatty/MTG-Scanner
MIT License

Adapted:
  - Capture UI flow (frontend/src/features/scanner/ScannerPage.tsx): guide
    frame the user aligns a card to, capture, identify, add-to-collection.
  - Scryfall-ID-centric result shape for adding a scanned card to a
    collection.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copies of both projects' MIT license text are available at their
respective repositories linked above.
